# Add comprehensive tests for required parts enforcement

New test files:

1. itr-compiler/src/test/scala/itrcompiler/application/services/RequiredPartsValidationTest.scala
   - validateBatch should pass when all required parts present
   - validateBatch should fail when ARCH missing
   - validateBatch should fail when LEGEND missing
   - validateBatch should fail when VERIFICATION missing
   - validateBatch should fail when E2EVERIFICATION missing
   - validateBatch should fail when multiple parts missing
   - validateForSingleCU should pass when folder has all parts
   - validateForSingleCU should pass when current CU creates missing part
   - validateForSingleCU should fail when folder missing parts and CU does not create them
   - validateForSingleCU should handle empty folder correctly

2. itr-compiler/src/test/scala/itrcompiler/integration/RequiredPartsEnforcementTest.scala
   - Batch compilation should fail without ARCH
   - Batch compilation should fail without LEGEND
   - Batch compilation should fail without VERIFICATION
   - Batch compilation should fail without E2EVERIFICATION
   - Batch compilation should succeed with all required parts
   - Single CU compilation should fail if folder empty and CU is regular
   - Single CU compilation should succeed if folder has all parts
   - Single CU compilation should succeed if CU creates missing part

3. itr-compiler/src/test/scala/itrcompiler/integration/BatchWithRequiredPartsTest.scala
   - JSON batch with ARCH, LEGEND, VERIFICATION, E2EVERIFICATION
   - YAML batch with ARCH, LEGEND, VERIFICATION, E2EVERIFICATION
   - Verify all files created with correct names

4. Update itr-compiler/src/test/scala/itrcompiler/infrastructure/parsers/JSONFormatTest.scala
